<%# locals: (line:) %>
<%# How much of what an envelope had to spend is Available, as a bar under its name on the month view, as wide as the name's column: primary for plenty, warning for a little, a dashed line in error for Overspent, and none at all when it had nothing to spend. It has no word, since the Available figure is the text (components/available_pill), so it's hidden from assistive technology. %>
<%# Plenty is blue and not green, so it's never told from Overspent's red by hue alone, which someone who can't tell red from green can't do, and each level has a shape of its own as well: Overspent is dashed, and the pill around Available has an icon. A native <progress> because its length is a value, where a styled div's would need an inline style attribute; Overspent is always a full line, so it's an SVG of dashes, clipped to the bar's rounded ends wherever the last dash falls. %>
<%# The slot is the same height at every level, even with no bar, and as tall as the word Overspent under the pill, so no level changes a row's height. %>
<% level = line.available_level %>
<div class="flex h-3 items-center" aria-hidden="true">
  <% case level %>
  <% when :plenty, :little %>
    <progress class="progress <%= level == :plenty ? "progress-primary" : "progress-warning" %> block w-full" value="<%= line.available_percent %>" max="100" aria-hidden="true"></progress>
  <% when :overspent %>
    <svg class="block h-2 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-box text-error" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="0" y1="4" x2="100%" y2="4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="8" stroke-dasharray="12 4" /></svg>
  <% end %>
</div>
